]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>The instability of a spin glass phase against an external magnetic field is discussed on the basis of a Landau\u2010type theory of phase transition with two order parameters. There are two different critical magnetic fields, both approaching zero for <jats:italic>T<\/jats:italic> \u2192 <jats:italic>T<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>SG<\/jats:sub>; the principal meaning of these critical fields is considered. The free energy <jats:italic>F<\/jats:italic>(<jats:italic>H, T<\/jats:italic>) develops different branches as a function of <jats:italic>H<\/jats:italic> and <jats:italic>T<\/jats:italic> with bifurcations typical for non\u2010equilibrium phase transitions (or dynamical instabilities).<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/pssb.2220900206","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2007,7,10]],"date-time":"2007-07-10T11:06:56Z","timestamp":1184065616000},"page":"475-485","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":5,"title":["Spin glass transition. A dynamical instability"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"90","author":[{"given":"D.","family":"Deutges","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"A.","family":"Freudenhammer","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"G.","family":"Heber","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2006,2,8]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_1_2_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063\/1.30084"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_3_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/978-1-4615-8912-9"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_3_3","volume-title":"Cooperative Effects","author":"Haken H.","year":"1974"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_4_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1143\/PTP.58.1151"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_5_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088\/0022-3719\/10\/24\/009"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_6_2","doi-assert